# Pin LF for every text file in the repo.
#
# The reproducible-build verification F-Droid runs against our v1.0 APK
# failed once because `assets/workouts_sample.json` shipped with CRLF
# bytes from a Windows-built APK while F-Droid's Linux build produced
# the same JSON with LF — gradle bundles assets verbatim from the
# working tree, and Windows checkouts with `core.autocrlf=true` get
# CRLF in the working tree even though the index is LF.
#
# This pins LF unconditionally so any contributor's working tree
# matches what gets checked in, regardless of OS or autocrlf config.
# Anything bundled into the APK (assets/*) or read at build time is
# safe.
#
# After landing this file, run `git add --renormalize .` once to
# refresh existing working trees.
* text=auto eol=lf
